                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="org_1010">Staveley, Derbyshire.
                        Parish church of St Mary</orgName><p><q>Orate pro anime magistre <persName
                              role="fmo" key="person_3993">Roberti Bartram</persName> qui hunc
                           librum dedit Ecclesie Sancte Marie de Staveley ad orandum specialiter pro
                           anima eiusdem Bartram ex pro animabus uxoris sue et domini Thome Bartram
                           ex parentum suorum et pro animabus omnium aliorum benefactorum pro quibus
                           ipse in vita sua tenebatur orare ... et dedit ecclesie sub condicione
                           quod rector ejusdem ecclesie ex parte boreali habeat usum eiusdem in
                           perpetuum</q>. Copy (s. xix) in London, British Library, Additional MS
                        6668 fols. 151-2 of a transcript made in 1705. See <title>Derbyshire
                           Archaeological and Natural History Society Journal</title>, 32 (1911), p.
                        167.</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Richard Hall of Dronfield in 1705. This was
                     the last known provenance according to the second edition of Medieval Libraries
                     of Great Britain (1964), p. 223. The book remains untraced.</provenance>
               </history>
